<title>PHILIPPINES: PAL stewards threaten to strike over wage package.</title>
<headline>PAL stewards threaten to strike over wage package.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flight attendants of Philippine Airlines (PAL) threatened on Thursday to go on strike over delay in negotiations for a new wage package.</p>
<p>&quot;We feel that our options are getting fewer each day,&quot; the Flight Attendants and Stewards Association of the Philippines (FASAP) said in a statement.</p>
<p>The threat comes less than a week after PAL ground crew ended a three-day strike over pay which stranded thousands of domestic and international flight passengers.</p>
<p>FASAP said flight attendants had had no pay increase for four years.</p>
<p>PAL officials were unavailable to comment.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
